   "snap_m": 1,
   "how": "The downstream tip of Temple Island, as OS OpenMap Local (October 2026) draws the island, moved onto the OS Open Rivers line. Henley Royal Regatta says its course runs \"from below the Berkshire side of Temple Island\". The organiser's page says \"the official regatta start\".",
   "sure": "About 60 m either way. The start pontoons were not located."
  },
  "finish": {
   "lat": 51.54032,
   "lon": -0.90011,
   "snap_m": 0,
   "how": "2,112 m upstream of the start along the OS Open Rivers line. That is 311 m downstream of Henley Bridge (Historic England list entries 1369131 and 1117419). Henley Royal Regatta names the finish Poplar Point, which no open-licence dataset used here places.",
   "sure": "About 100 m either way: the start's 60 m, and the OS line being simpler than the river."
  }
 },
